Fix $\alpha\in\mathbb R$ and $r<u<r_+$. As $\beta\to+\infty$ through real values,
\begin{equation}
  W^{(r)}_{\alpha,\beta}=r^{-\beta}H_{\alpha,r}(\beta)+O_{\alpha,r,u}(u^{-\beta}),
\end{equation}
where the following function has period $2$ and is bounded above and away from zero:
\[
 H_{\alpha,r}(\beta)=\frac{1}{1-r^{-2}}
   \sum_{t\in\mathcal T_r}\frac{r^{\beta-2\lceil(\beta+2\alpha-1-D_\alpha(t))/2\rceil}}{t^2}.
\]
In particular $W^{(r)}_{\alpha,\beta+2}/W^{(r)}_{\alpha,\beta}\to r^{-2}$.
